A('thm-temperley-lieb-diagram-category-laws','Finite stack component counts prove associativity, strict juxtaposition and the central scalar-map algebra structure.',empty=C('The object0 has the empty matching as identity; juxtaposition with it leaves every boundary labeling unchanged in the unit argument.'),zero=C('A stack carries delta to its nonnegative loop count; none of the associativity or unit comparisons divides by delta, so delta0 and the zero ring remain allowed.'),one=C('The sole rank-one matching is its vertical identity; the same stack and empty-unit arguments apply with no elementary generator.'),degenerate=C('Odd boundary sums give zero morphism modules and composition remains bilinear into them; no matching or nonzero scalar is selected to prove the axioms.'),endpoints=C('The domain/codomain labels include0, and the object-addition associativity and empty-unit proof explicitly preserves those endpoints.'),**{'nonempty-choice':N('Each composite and juxtaposition is determined by given finite matchings and labels; the category-law verification makes no arbitrary-family selection.')})
A('thm-temperley-lieb-diagrams-have-catalan-cardinality','Opening/closing endpoints and stack pairing give inverse finite bijections with balanced words and Dyck paths, so the diagram count is Catalan.',empty=C('At n0 the empty pairing corresponds to the empty word and empty Dyck path, giving the single rank-zero basis diagram.'),zero=C('The count concerns the matching basis before multiplication; delta0 changes loop coefficients but does not identify distinct basis matchings.'),one=C('At n1 the word is one opening followed by its closing, and the only matching is the vertical strand, so the Catalan count is1.'),degenerate=C('The basis count is a bijection of finite sets and remains the free-module rank over the stated ring without a semisimplicity or delta-invertibility premise.'),endpoints=C('The counting assertion includes n0; zero semilength is represented by the empty encoding, not removed from the Catalan formula.'),**{'nonempty-choice':N('The left-to-right stack gives the inverse pairing algorithm uniquely, so no representatives or arbitrary bijection are chosen.')})
A('thm-temperley-lieb-generator-normal-form','Jones normal words span by explicit TL reductions and their index sequences are counted by path corners.',empty=C('With n0 there are no generator indices; the sole empty word represents the scalar unit and the empty path.'),zero=C('The rewriting uses multiplication by loop coefficients, not their inverses; delta0 can delete terms but leaves the spanning assertion valid.'),one=C('At n1 the generator range is empty and the normal-word list consists of the unit, as required for Catalan number1.'),degenerate=C('Normal-word spanning is over the arbitrary coefficient ring and claims no generic semisimplicity or division by delta.'),endpoints=C('The allowed descending blocks respect1<=j<=i<n; empty block lists handle the lower ranks and the identity word.'),**{'nonempty-choice':N('The reduction and corner/path encodings are finite procedures on a supplied word, not choices from an unindexed family.')})
A('lem-temperley-lieb-generators-satisfy-local-relations','Stack path counts prove the square, both adjacent triples by horizontal reflection and disjoint-pair commutation.',empty=C('For n0 and n1 the generator and relation sets are empty; the final quotient map sends the scalar unit to the identity diagram.'),zero=C('At delta0 the one-loop square gives d_i squared0, while the triple reductions create no loop and remain valid.'),one=C('One elementary generator occurs first at n2; only its square relation is present, and adjacent triple ranges are empty.'),degenerate=C('The proof follows paths and counts loops and therefore does not require a field, a nonzero loop value or faithful representation.'),endpoints=C('Squares use1<=i<n, adjacent triples use1<=i<=n-2 and distant pairs require both indices valid; no endpoint generator outside the rank is used.'),**{'nonempty-choice':N('The specified cup/cap pairings and horizontal reflection determine all comparisons, with no basis or representative selection.')})
A('thm-temperley-lieb-diagram-generators-span','The finite matching is reduced by its arcs/through paths to a product of elementary cup-cap diagrams.',empty=C('At rank0 the empty matching is the unit, represented by the empty product of generators.'),zero=C('The constructive factorization produces the given matching without solving by an inverse power of delta, so the delta0 ring case stays in scope.'),one=C('At rank1 the only diagram is vertical identity and its factorization is the empty generator word.'),degenerate=C('The spanning construction uses finite noncrossing pairings over the given ring, rather than a dimension comparison over a generic field.'),endpoints=C('Generator positions belong to adjacent boundary pairs in1,...,n; if no arc move remains the vertical matching ends the construction.'),**{'nonempty-choice':N('A prescribed finite matching supplies the paths and arcs used in the factorization; no unrestricted collection of witnesses is chosen.')})
A('thm-temperley-lieb-presentation-isomorphism','Surjectivity on matching diagrams and equal positive finite Catalan ranks give a square matrix with right inverse; its determinant is a unit, proving independence.',empty=C('At n0 the identity empty matching makes the Catalan rank1, so the proof uses a1-by-1 matrix rather than an unsupported size-zero determinant criterion.'),zero=C('The determinant-unit argument works over the arbitrary commutative ring, and no loop parameter inverse occurs even when delta0.'),one=C('At n1 the sole empty generator word maps to the vertical diagram; the rank comparison again has Catalan rank1.'),degenerate=C('Surjective square matrices over the given commutative ring have unit determinant via the constructed right inverse; spanning alone is not used to infer independence.'),endpoints=C('The identity diagram ensures the finite rank is positive at every n>=0, including both low-rank generator-free cases.'),**{'nonempty-choice':C('The right inverse selects preimages only for one finite diagram basis; the proof makes finitely many selections, without an arbitrary-family choice axiom.')})
