A('lem-temperley-lieb-link-state-gram-form-is-invariant','Reflection reverses the stack and the coefficient of the full-through identity gives the same loop count on both invariant-form sides.',empty=C('The empty state at n=t0 glues to the empty identity with coefficient delta^0=1_R.'),zero=C('At delta0 the value remains1_R for a zero-loop full-propagation composite and is0 for a positive loop count; invariance uses the same count on each side.'),one=C('At n=t1 the single through path gives unit pairing and identity action, satisfying the invariant-form equality.'),degenerate=C('The form may have a radical or vanish; symmetry and invariance are proved without assuming nondegeneracy.'),endpoints=C('The all-defect tn case and perfect-matching t0 case both use the coefficient-of-identity rule, including the empty t0 identity.'),**{'nonempty-choice':N('Each basis pair has a fixed reflected composite; bilinear extension determines the form and involves no arbitrary selection.')})
A('lem-temperley-lieb-link-state-restriction-filtration','The rightmost-defect submodule and cut-arc quotient give the all-ring exact sequence; only the additional noncritical complex branch splits.',zero=C('The basis maps and generator check in steps1.1–3.1 divide by no loop value, so the sequence includes delta0.'),one=C('At n1,t1 the sequence is W00 mapping isomorphically to the restricted one-dimensional state and an out-of-range zero quotient.'),**{'nonempty-choice':C('The first maps are specified basis bijections. The complex splitting chooses a single square root v of q and finite pairing vectors; its central element is independent of the sign of v, and no infinite-family choice is used.')})
A('prop-temperley-lieb-link-state-form-vanishes-exactly-at-zero-loop-without-defects','For nonzero R, explicit no-loop pairs at positive t and a one-loop pair at t0 prove the vanishing criterion; the empty state has unit pairing.',empty=C('The separate n=t0 computation gives pairing1_R, which is nonzero since R is nonzero, so the empty state is excluded from the vanishing branch.'),zero=C('When t0,n>0 every overlay has at least one loop and delta0 kills all entries; the constructed one-loop overlay detects nonzero delta.'),one=C('With a0 and t>0, the all-defect state pairs with itself as1_R; this includes the one-strand label.'),degenerate=C('R must be nonzero: over the zero ring even the empty unit form is zero. The proof needs delta itself nonzero, not invertible, to exhibit a nonzero t0 entry.'),endpoints=C('The proof separates t>0, t0 with positive even n, and n=t0, exhausting the admissible defect endpoints.'),**{'nonempty-choice':N('The witnesses are the specified adjacent-cup and shifted-cup patterns; no arbitrary pairing is selected.')})
A('thm-temperley-lieb-link-state-diagram-basis-is-cellular','Cutting each through strand gives inverse pairs of link states; reflection and propagation ideals prove the cellular axioms. The phrase exactly when prescribes the label order r<=t, not a biconditional characterization of cellular algebras.',empty=C('Rank0 has the empty matching with t0 and its single pair of empty link states; the cellular basis consists of the unit.'),zero=C('Multiplication at delta0 is still triangular by propagation and loop-count coefficients; no coefficient inverse is used.'),one=C('At rank1 the through diagram is the only cellular basis vector and its involution and scalar cell module are the identity ones.'),degenerate=C('Cellularity is established over the given ring without assuming a nondegenerate cell form or semisimple algebra.'),endpoints=C('The label set contains every t of parity n between0 and n; perfect matchings and all-through diagrams are included in the cut construction.'),**{'nonempty-choice':N('The top/bottom decomposition is recovered from the given matching; the cellular data do not require arbitrary basis choices.')})
A('cor-temperley-lieb-nonzero-cell-forms-classify-simple-modules','Applying the cellular head theorem classifies the nonzero form quotients; an identically zero form gives quotient0 but says nothing about the module actual head.',empty=C('At rank0 the scalar algebra has the empty-state unit form, so its sole form quotient is the one-dimensional simple module.'),zero=C('If the form is identically zero, its radical is the entire module and D=0; this does not erase an actual nonzero module head.'),one=C('The single all-defect state has form1 and gives a nonzero simple quotient; this includes the rank-one algebra.'),degenerate=C('The corollary assumes a field for absolute simplicity and unique maximal radical; it does not extend that classification to arbitrary coefficient rings.'),endpoints=C('The t0 form may vanish while the tn all-defect form is unit; the classification discards only zero form quotients, not the allowed labels themselves.'),**{'nonempty-choice':N('The argument applies the cellular theorem to the fixed matching basis; it chooses no representatives or additional simple labels.')})
